    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="0419" n="333" xml:id="pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.91/12–844</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warm
                                Springs, Georgia</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-08">December 8, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the Secretary of State</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I think this Soviet-Iranian matter should be taken up by Harriman with Stalin in person. The Teheran agreement was pretty definite and
                    my contribution was to suggest to Stalin
                    and Churchill that three or four Trustees
                    build a new port in Iran at the head of the Persian Gulf (free port), take over
                    the whole railroad from there into Russia, and run the thing for the good of
                    all. Stalin’s comment was merely that it
                    was an interesting idea and he offered no objection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D.
                                R[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
